Because ([2](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2607.01203v1#S3.E2 "In III Preliminaries and Problem Statement ‣ GPU-Parallel Linearization Error Bounds for Real-Time Robust Optimal Control of Nonlinear and Neural Network Dynamics")) is an intractable infinite-dimensional problem, RNOCP solvers often simplify it by computing (A) a nominal state-input trajectory and (B) a tracking controller around that trajectory. In this paper, we use one such method, GPUSLS [[10](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2607.01203v1#bib.bib10)], which adapts [[9](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2607.01203v1#bib.bib9)] for real-time solution on the GPU. We then extend [[10](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2607.01203v1#bib.bib10)] to account for linearization error in Sec. [V](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2607.01203v1#S5 "V Using Linearization Error Bounds in GPUSLS ‣ GPU-Parallel Linearization Error Bounds for Real-Time Robust Optimal Control of Nonlinear and Neural Network Dynamics"). Our approach uses SLS, which we now review.

