### IV-D Differentiable, Parallel Bound Implementation

We implement our LEBs in JAX, with the PBH using immrax for interval arithmetic and jax\_verify providing CROWN-based bounds for NN dynamics. JAX offers differentiability and GPU parallelization, enabling *gradient-based refinement* of the nominal point 𝜶~\tilde{\bm{\alpha}} and scalable *input domain partitioning* to reduce conservativeness for SLS.

