### V-B Efficient SLS Implementation on the GPU

We propose GPUSLS-Linearization Error Optimization (GPUSLS-LEO), which builds on GPUSLS [[10](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2607.01203v1#bib.bib10)] to explicitly account for linearization error propagation. We first replace the ellipsoidal disturbance representation of [[10](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2607.01203v1#bib.bib10)] with a zonotope, modifying the constraint tightenings and cost terms via ([29](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2607.01203v1#S5.E29 "In V-A Nonlinear SLS Formulation ‣ V Using Linearization Error Bounds in GPUSLS ‣ GPU-Parallel Linearization Error Bounds for Real-Time Robust Optimal Control of Nonlinear and Neural Network Dynamics"))-([31](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2607.01203v1#S5.E31 "In V-A Nonlinear SLS Formulation ‣ V Using Linearization Error Bounds in GPUSLS ‣ GPU-Parallel Linearization Error Bounds for Real-Time Robust Optimal Control of Nonlinear and Neural Network Dynamics")). At each controller update, we modify GPUSLS by including a zonotopic bound on the linearization error via ([25](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2607.01203v1#S5.E25 "In V-A Nonlinear SLS Formulation ‣ V Using Linearization Error Bounds in GPUSLS ‣ GPU-Parallel Linearization Error Bounds for Real-Time Robust Optimal Control of Nonlinear and Neural Network Dynamics")). We then modify the initialization of 𝚽x\mathbf{\Phi}^{\text{x}} via ([34c](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2607.01203v1#S5.E34.3 "In 34 ‣ V-A Nonlinear SLS Formulation ‣ V Using Linearization Error Bounds in GPUSLS ‣ GPU-Parallel Linearization Error Bounds for Real-Time Robust Optimal Control of Nonlinear and Neural Network Dynamics")).

